{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 RefLab\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Comparaison mix / references dans REAPER, en JSFX (compatible REAPER portable).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab 4 references, chargees depuis {\f1 <REAPER>/Data/references}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Spectre mix + reference superposes, courbe d'ecart, vitesse de mesure reglable\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Isolation de bandes (5 bandes) et modes d'ecoute stereo / mono / side / G / D\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab LUFS momentary / short-term / integre (BS.1770), match loudness automatique\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Boucle par reference (glisser sur la forme d'onde)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Tous les reglages assignables en MIDI (Param > Learn) ou via les actions "RefLab - ..."\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A placer dans le Monitoring FX. Le paquet {\b Todoroki Companion} ajoute l'ouverture du dossier des references et la mise a jour automatique de la liste.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 RS Trig Sampler\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Drum replacement sampler in JSFX (portable REAPER friendly), meant to sit after a trigger (MIDI) tool. One instance = one drum element, up to 8 samples played in parallel.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab 8 slots, each with multi-velocity / round-robin kits (.rsk.wav) or plain audio files\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Per slot: volume, pan, pitch, attack / hold / decay / curve, velocity target + sensitivity, voices, round robin cycle / random, choke groups, 8 stereo outputs, mute / solo\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Samples are stored in the project and in REAPER presets (one preset = a full layered kit)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Library in {\f1 <REAPER>/Data/RSampler}, filled by the {\b RS Trig Kit Builder} script (Slate Trigger 2 .tci import, WAV folders, auto-organised by element / instrument)\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
